<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick V of the Palatinate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1596">1596</a>–<a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Winter King</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick V was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a> and the leading Calvinist prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. In 1619 he accepted the crown of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> from the Protestant rebels against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>, but his army was crushed at the White Mountain in 1620, earning him the name Winter King. He lost both Bohemia and his own lands and electoral vote, and died in exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-v-of-the-palatinate.jpg" alt="Frederick V of the Palatinate" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michiel Jansz. van Mierevelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich_V._von_der_Pfalz_bis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
